  "notes": "Formed from {導|どう} (to lead, guide) + {電|でん} (electricity). Most often seen in the compound {導電性|どうでんせい} (electrical conductivity).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {導電|どうでん}⟦{性|せい}→性：09880_sei⟧: electrical conductivity\n- {導電|どうでん}⟦{体|たい}→体：09872_tai⟧: conductor (of electricity)\n- {導電|どうでん}⟦{材料|ざいりょう}→材料：02831_zairyou⟧: conductive material\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{絶縁|ぜつえん}→絶縁：08374_zetsuen⟧: insulation — the opposite property, blocking current\n- ⟦{通電|つうでん}→通電：30050_tsuuden⟧: energizing — passing current through a circuit to power it",
